"The prognosis is influenced by several documented factors. Favorable findings include negative surgical margins and absence of lymph node metastasis, alongside the seminal vesicles not being invaded. The preoperative PSA was 3.7. Conversely, the documented Gleason 4+5 (ISUP grade group 5) and pT3a stage contribute to increased risk. The absence of lymph node metastasis is a positive finding. Missing biopsy grade information introduces uncertainty regarding the true tumor biology compared to the resection specimen. The nodal status is documented as negative, which is reassuring. The primary uncertainty lies in the postoperative PSA and its subsequent trajectory, as previous notes are absent. Information regarding postoperative PSA levels and their trend is crucial for refining the prognosis. The fixed estimated horizon is 62.79 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 47.09–78.49 months; its coverage has not been validated."
